Hi,

there are currently three search boxes on the website. That's at least one too 
many, as the search box with the dropdown menu can perform the same search the 
"search page titles" box does.
I suggest removing the "search page titles" box and keeping the customized 
google search and the wiki search, or maybe removing the wiki search as well.

Another thing is, that la xris made firefox search plugins for jboski and 
jbovlaste. If we included two lines in the <head> of the lojban wiki site, 
firefox would suggest adding those as "search engines" in the search engines 
dropdown list. Using an extension like ConQuery could come in handy for marking 
a word in a website and looking it up on jbovlaste, or marking a sentence bau la 
lojban and have it validated/glossed via jboski.

Tell me what you think.
   - Timo


